wash (0.22.0-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * wash-login (security): the default su backend accepted wrong
    passwords. Run as root (the supervisord example, sudo wash-login,
    wash-vmlogin without --autologin), su never asks for a password, so
    any password logged in as any user. su now runs with nobody's real
    uid when wash-login is root, and an su that succeeds without having
    been sent the password is a rejection. Separately, the tty the
    password crossed edited it before PAM saw it, so "pw" followed by a
    newline and junk, or with DEL / ^U / ^W edits, checked as "pw";
    passwords with control characters are now refused. The systemd unit
    (User=wash-system) was not open to the first; upgrade anyway.
  * Clipboard: two slots, the way X11 does it (docs/CLIPBOARD.md). The
    clipboard is what you copied (Ctrl+C/X/V, the menus; Ctrl+V is the
    browser's native paste, so it works over plain HTTP); the selection
    is what you last highlighted, held by the router, pasted with
    middle-click, Alt+right-click or left+right. Highlighting no longer
    wipes the clipboard. Right-click is the wash menu everywhere,
    terminals included; Shift+right-click is the browser's. In a
    terminal, Ctrl+Shift+V sends ^V and a pasted image is saved on the
    router's host and its path pasted. The sidebar Clipboard pane shows
    both slots.
  * Screensaver: on by default, Harbor Night. A config that turned it
    off keeps it off.
  * Shell head: it follows the tab in use. A background tab's redial no
    longer takes it, so "Use here" stops coming back; a tab without the
    head shows a thin band across the top.

